More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (901–910)
901. Improper Validation of Login API Responses
Login API Information Disclosure
Login responses reveal whether usernames exist, helping attackers enumerate accounts.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
902. Insecure Handling of User Group Management
User Group Authorization Bypass
Attackers add themselves to privileged groups without authorization.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
903. Improper Validation of Document Preview APIs
Document Preview Data Exposure
Preview endpoints reveal sensitive document data.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
904. Insecure Handling of User Feedback Systems
Feedback System Injection
Attackers inject malicious content into feedback forms.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
905. Improper Validation of Audit Report Exports
Audit Report Data Exposure
Audit reports can be downloaded by unauthorized users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
906. Insecure Handling of Event Logging APIs
Event Log Exposure
Event logging systems expose sensitive internal information.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
907. Improper Validation of User Verification APIs
User Verification Bypass
Attackers bypass identity verification mechanisms.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
908. Insecure Handling of Payment Notification Systems
Payment Notification Manipulation
Attackers send fake payment notifications to manipulate system behavior.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
909. Improper Validation of Team Collaboration APIs
Team Collaboration Authorization Bypass
Attackers access team resources belonging to other organizations.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
910. Insecure Handling of Data Synchronization APIs
Data Sync Authorization Bypass
